   "body": "Fixes #332085\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds the BYOK language-model bridge between a window's renderer and an Agent Host that runs in a Remote-WSL server, so a `Custom Endpoint` / BYOK model configured in the window can be selected and used by the native Agents window when the Agent Host is remote.\n\nBefore this change the BYOK handler existed only inside the window's own process: a remote Agent Host saw the capability as absent and the BYOK models never reached the model picker of the Agents window.\n\n## Design\n\n- `src/vs/platform/agentHost/common/agentHostByokLmProtocol.ts` (new): the private AHP method names, the metadata key and the runtime shape validators for the bridge. It is private protocol, not a public extension API: no contribution point, command or `package.json` API is added or changed.\n- `agentHostExtensionProtocol.ts`: one capability flag and the bridge meta/command entries, so an extension host can advertise and negotiate the bridge the same way the existing chat-state and worktree capabilities do.\n- `protocolServerHandler.ts`: registers the per-connection bridge, relays `resolveModel` and the chat-request calls to the registered handler, and removes the registration when the connection or the handler goes away. A connection that never advertised the capability, a disconnected handler and an unknown call are all refused instead of queued.\n- `byokLmBridgeRegistry.ts` / `agentHostServerMain.ts`: the standalone server keeps its own handler registry; the wiring is a registry lookup, no new state owner.\n- `agentHostClientByokLmChannel.ts`: the renderer's throttled model-snapshot stream moves out of the channel class into the exported `createAgentHostByokLmModelSnapshotEvent()`, so the AHP bridge and the in-process reverse channel publish the same snapshot from one implementation; the channel calls it instead of owning it.\n- Tests: the new bridge cases live in `test/node/protocolServerHandler.test.ts` (dispatch, refusal of an unadvertised or disconnected handler, cleanup), `test/electron-browser/agentHostProtocolClient.test.ts` (registration gating on the advertised capability, snapshot publish, unregister on disposal) and `chat/test/browser/remoteAgentHost/remoteAgentHostChatContribution.test.ts` (the handler is registered on every connection).\n- `agentService.ts`: `registerByokLmHandler?` on the agent-host client surface.\n- `agentHostProtocolClient.ts` + `remoteAgentHostChatContribution.ts`: the renderer side registers the handler over its existing AHP connection, keeps its remembered-credential and entitlement gates exactly where they are (the credential never crosses into the Agent Host process), and handles the model snapshot updates in place, including reconnect and disposal.\n- `serviceBootstrapping.md`: documents the data flow, the per-connection cleanup and the renderer credential/policy boundary.\n\n## How to test?\n\n```sh\n# node lane (protocol server handler, includes the new bridge cases)\npnpm run test-node --run src/vs/platform/agentHost/test/node/protocolServerHandler.test.ts\n\n# browser lane (renderer contribution, including the new BYOK handler cases)\npnpm run test-browser-no-install -- --run src/vs/workbench/contrib/chat/test/browser/remoteAgentHost/remoteAgentHostChatContribution.test.ts --browser chromium\n\n# electron-browser lane (renderer protocol client)\n./scripts/test.sh --run src/vs/platform/agentHost/test/electron-browser/agentHostProtocolClient.test.ts\n```\n\nThe recorded totals are from those runs on `main` at `edc9152`:\nnode `519` passing, browser `13` passing, electron-browser `432` passing. The\n`electron-browser` directory is collected only by `test/unit/electron/index.js`\n(the node and browser runners exclude it), which is why that lane is the one\nthat exercises `agentHostProtocolClient.test.ts`.\nManual: in a Remote-WSL window with a BYOK `Custom Endpoint` provider whose endpoint is reachable from the WSL distro, open the Agents window and select the BYOK model; the model is listed, the request streams, and the Agent Host process holds no credential (checkpoint in `serviceBootstrapping.md`).\n\n## Does this introduce a change that needs to be updated with docs?\n\nNo documentation change beyond `src/vs/platform/agentHost/node/serviceBootstrapping.md`; the change is internal protocol plumbing and adds no user-facing setting or command.\n",
